  "body": "[*As mentioned by @DMRobertson,*](https://matrix.to/#/!SGNQGPGUwtcPBUotTL:matrix.org/$Em8UxrFvoDCOrvws0YyM14itO_DwWHJvvN9S0MkzzGw?via=jki.re&via=matrix.org&via=element.io)\r\n\r\nWe should report the currently running version as a metric.\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\n\r\nIt's hard to tell what the `matrix.org` deployment was running over time in order to correlate regressions.\r\n\r\nThe best we have seems to be to go log-diving in the internal ops Matrix room with a bunch of alerts and hope someone posted the commit hash at the time of the deploy.\r\n\r\n### Dev notes\r\n\r\nWe have `SYNAPSE_VERSION` which looks like `1.84.0rc1 (b=matrix-org-hotfixes,184a688c64)` and includes a lot of useful information which looks perfect to report.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n - https://jorgelbg.me/2019/02/display-the-applications-version-in-your-grafana-dashboards/\r\n - https://www.robustperception.io/exposing-the-software-version-to-prometheus/\r\n - https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/issues/2227\r\n - https://www.etsy.com/codeascraft/track-every-release/\r\n - https://stackoverflow.com/questions/50415659/tracking-events-with-prometheus-and-grafana",
